# One line ending in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# Git on Windows checks text files out as CRLF by default. Two of the files
# here are compiled into the binary with `include_str!` — the sample screenplay
# and the English language file — so a CRLF checkout produced a Windows build
# that embedded different bytes from the macOS and Linux ones, and behaved
# differently for it. `--self-check` caught it; this is what stops it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The font is bytes, not text, and must never be touched.
*.ttf binary
